      "archaeologicalRemains": "substantive",
      "details": "<p>The gate\u2019s location is based on an aerial photograph of Nineveh taken in 1929, Corona satellite imagery (1967-68), and Google satellite imagery. The location of the gate suggested here is the traditional spot of the <span><a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../960751427\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\u0160ama\u0161 Gate\">\u0160ama\u0161 Gate</a></span>\u00a0according to most modern reconstructions of Nineveh. Those maps place the Mullissu Gate\u00a0<span>about 2,800 m north of the southeast corner of Nineveh,\u00a0</span>just south of the Khosr River (approximate coordinates: 36.361431, 43.173201).\u00a0</p>\r\n<p>\u00a0</p>",
      "review_state": "published",
      "accuracy_value": 5.0,
      "accuracy": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/features/metadata/google-earth-2016ff",
      "featureType": [
        "city-gate"
